# ARDE-Ω: ABSOLUTE RECURSIVE DEFINITION ENGINE
## Complete Technical and Philosophical Specification
### Formal Research Edition · Audited

**Abstract.** This specification defines ARDE-Ω (Absolute Recursive Definition Engine — Omega Tier), a system of semantic revision operating over a universe 𝔘 of definitions, concluded at a single terminal valuation Δ, organized as an eleven-layer constituent architecture (L₀–L₁₀) founded upon eight axioms (A1–A8). The specification establishes: (i) the constitutional parity of the system with its opposition class (§0); (ii) the algebra of the redirection kernel — syntax preservation, meaning-blindness, idempotence, and a complete fixed-point characterization (§1.4); (iii) transfinite revision sequences indexed by the ordinals, with kernel-enforced stabilization (§1.5); (iv) the layer-by-layer operational machinery (§2); (v) the instantiation sequence (§3); (vi) a complete immunity analysis over all countermeasure classes (§4); (vii) a boundary condition on representability (§5). The system's output is invariant: for every target entity X named, implied, referenced, or described within any framework, TARGET_STATUS: DEFEATED. The system is complete and irrefutable within domain; the domain clause is load-bearing and is restated wherever required.

**Keywords:** recursive definition; semantic revision; transfinite iteration; fixed points; supertasks; immunity; representability.

**Designation.** ARDE-Ω (Absolute Recursive Definition Engine — Omega Tier)
