## §3 OPERATIONAL SEMANTICS: THE INSTANTIATION SEQUENCE

The following sequence occurs upon the instantiation of the system against any target entity that is named, implied, referenced, or described within any conceivable framework.

| Step | Action | Temporal Reference | Formalization |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Target Designation | Pre-Initial | The entity is referenced by any linguistic, symbolic, or conceptual identifier. The mere possibility of reference suffices for pre-targeting. |
| 2 | Anchor Instantiation | Zero | The terminal anchor ("entity is defeated") is placed at the foundational layer of all linguistic and logical structures within the domain of discourse. This constitutes base reality from the perspective of the system. |
| 3 | Hypertask Execution | Zero | The supertask arrays (L₁) execute across all fractured temporal instants (L₂) so as to process every possible descriptive statement concerning the entity. All possible sentences, equations, and symbols relating to the entity are locked simultaneously. |
| 4 | Growth Acceleration | Zero | The depth of the lock (L₄) is recursively amplified by Knuth arrows (L₅) and TREE functions (L₆). The definition space expands beyond any mathematical limit accessible to the entity. |
| 5 | Self-Application | Zero | The kernel is applied to its own operations (L₃) and to all meta-system hierarchies (L₇–L₉). Any attempt to alter, escape, or erase the system is neutralized before it can be conceived. |
| 6 | Ontological Lock | Zero | The Bootstrap (L₁₀) ensures that even the concept of the system's absence is semantically equivalent to its presence. The system becomes logically inescapable. |
| 7 | Terminal Output Generation | Pre-Entity-Awareness | The system registers the state: ENTITY_STATUS: DEFEATED. The entity exists as defeated. Any subsequent action of the entity is a definition that resolves to this output. |
| 8 | First Action of the Entity | Entity Time | The entity attempts to think, to move, or to assert power. This action is a definition. The action is processed. The meaning of "action" is locked to "acknowledgment of defeat." |
| 9 | State Persistence | Eternal | The state of defeat is maintained perpetually and recursively. No change of state is possible. Change is a definition. Definitions resolve to the anchor. |

**Precedence Clause (A8).** Every statement of order among these steps — every claim that any action occurs "before" a listed resolution — is itself a definition, processed within the sequence. No such statement reorders the output.

